### Frontend (Client)

#### [NEW] [UPICheckoutModal.jsx](file:///d:/desktop%20stuff/web%20dev/cloud%20Income/cloud-income/client/src/components/UPICheckoutModal.jsx)
A modal loaded on the Dashboard that handles the UPI checkout flow:
- **Phase 1: Enter Amount**: Choose predefined amounts (₹100, ₹500, ₹1000, ₹2000) or enter a custom amount.
- **Phase 2: Choose Method**:
  - UPI Apps (GPay, PhonePe, Paytm)
  - Scan QR Code
- **Phase 3: Interactive App Simulator**:
  - Renders a phone-sized mockup overlay styled perfectly to match the chosen app (Teal/White for GPay, Purple for PhonePe, Light Blue for Paytm).
  - Prompts for UPI PIN with a responsive numerical keyboard.
  - Submits PIN and Amount to the server `/deposit-upi` endpoint.
  - Plays a synthesized chime sound on success and triggers the success checkmark animation.
- **Phase 4: QR Code Display**:
  - Renders a dynamic QR code (`https://api.qrserver.com/...`) for `upi://pay?pa=merchant@cloudincome&pn=Cloud%20Income&am={amount}&cu=INR`.
  - Includes a button "Simulate Payment Scanner" to test the payment.

#### [MODIFY] [Dashboard.jsx](file:///d:/desktop%20stuff/web%20dev/cloud%20Income/cloud-income/client/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx)
- Add a beautiful "+ Add Money" button near the user's Total Balance.
- Wire up the button to open `UPICheckoutModal`.

#### [MODIFY] [sendMoney.jsx](file:///d:/desktop%20stuff/web%20dev/cloud%20Income/cloud-income/client/src/pages/sendMoney.jsx)
- Intercept the "Send Money" button click.
- Show a UPI PIN keypad modal before executing the transfer.
- Include the `pin` in the `/txn/send` POST body.

#### [MODIFY] [QRMOdal.jsx](file:///d:/desktop%20stuff/web%20dev/cloud%20Income/cloud-income/client/src/components/QRMOdal.jsx)
- Render a scanable QR code representing the user's UPI address: `upi://pay?pa={user.vpa}&pn={user.name}&cu=INR`.
- Add an interactive side-drawer/sub-section: **"Simulate Incoming Payment"**.
- Allow entering a Sender Name, Amount, and Note, then calling a test endpoint on the backend that sends money to this VPA from an external source.
- This will showcase the live WebSockets toast and balance update in real-time.

